[FINAL-TEXT] I have all the evidence needed. The picture is completely unambiguous.

**Summary of findings:**
- Ping from `host_1_1_1_1` → `web_server_0` (10.200.0.3): **0% packet loss** — path is healthy.
- DNS resolves `web0.local` → `10.200.0.3` correctly.
- OSPF on `router_core_1` has a valid route `10.200.0.0/24` via `router_core_3`.
- `curl http://web0.local` → **Connection refused on port 80**.
- `web_server_0` has **no listening sockets** except the Docker internal resolver.
- `systemctl status apache2` → **`Active: inactive (dead)`** — the service is enabled but not running. No journal entries.

---

```
=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: web_server_0
diagnosis_text:
The fault has nothing to do with OSPF or the core routing path. The network
is completely healthy: ICMP from host_1_1_1_1 reaches web_server_0
(10.200.0.3) with 0% packet loss, DNS correctly resolves web0.local to that
address, and router_core_1 holds a valid OSPF-learned route for
10.200.0.0/24 via router_core_3. Every hop in the data-plane forwarding path
is operational.

The actual fault is on web_server_0 itself: the Apache2 HTTP daemon is in
state "inactive (dead)". Although the unit is systemd-enabled (would start on
boot), it is not currently running, so port 80 has no listener. Any TCP
connection attempt is immediately reset by the kernel, producing the
"Connection refused" error that users observe when trying to load the portal.
This is why the page "never loads" — packets arrive at the server just fine,
but there is no process to accept them.

The root cause is that the apache2 service on web_server_0 has been stopped
(or crashed and not restarted) without leaving journal entries, indicating it
was manually stopped or the container was restarted without the service being
brought back up.

Corrective fix: On web_server_0, run `systemctl start apache2` (or
`service apache2 start`). Verify with `ss -tlnp | grep :80` that the port is
now listening, then re-test `curl http://web0.local` from host_1_1_1_1. No
routing or OSPF changes are needed.
=== END ===
```